Signature Rules (Must Read)
Signature Algorithm
MD5 encryption
Signature generation steps
1 .
Concatenate
the parameters of the unified request format into a string according to the following format.
appSecret={APP_SECRET}&channel={APP_ID}&content={加密后的业务参数}&timestamp={毫秒级时间戳}
2 .
Perform MD5 hash calculation on the concatenated string
3 .
Convert to lowercase hexadecimal string
Example
1 .
Assume the concatenated string is:
appSecret=3974076aff7b4f5da2998f437441745f&channel=10000&content=加密后的内容&timestamp=1678901234567
2 .
After MD5 hash calculation, the resulting signature value is:
e4d00b4bbc9fed7e16eb428ba0b3e6d5                                               
Verification steps
1 .
After receiving the request, the server extracts the appSecret, channel, content, and timestamp parameters from the request.
2 .
Concatenate strings using the same rules as the client:
3 .
appSecret={APP_SECRET}&channel={APP_ID}&content={encrypted content}×tamp={timestamp}
4 .
Perform an MD5 hash on the concatenated string and convert it to a lowercase hexadecimal string.
5 .
The calculated signature value is compared with the sign parameter carried in the request. If they match, the signature verification is successful; otherwise, the signature verification fails.

Business Parameter Encryption Rules (Must Read)
Encryption Algorithm
AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding
Algorithm: AES (Advanced Encryption Standard)
Operating mode: CBC (Cryptoblock Chaining)
Fill method: PKCS5Padding
Key: APP_SECRET is used as the key, issued by the platform.
Initialization Vector (IV): Initialization vector, issued by the platform.
Encryption steps
1 .
Convert the request content (a JSON-formatted string) into a byte array.
2 .
Encrypt the byte array using AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding mode.
3 .
The encrypted byte array is converted into a string using Base64 encoding, ultimately yielding the encrypted content.
Example
Assume the business parameters are as follows:
{
    "mchOrderId": "20240915123456",
    "amount": 5001,
    "channelCode": "PayPal",
    "customerName": "Alex",
    "email": "45615531941@google.com",
    "mobile": "45615531941",
    "notifyUrl": "https://www.google.com",
    "timestamp": 1678901234567
}
key: 3974076aff7b4f5da2998f437441745f
iv: 3175701037964796
After AES encryption and Base64 encoding, the encrypted content is as follows:

Decryption algorithm
1 .
Use the same key and initialization vector (IV) as the client.
2 .
Base64 decoding is performed on the content in the request to obtain an encrypted byte array.
3 .
The byte array is decrypted using AES/CBC/PKCS5Padding mode to obtain the original request content.

